        "original_id": "2c9f2860-cf46-5def-8b48-5639c2ff6527",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Warroad, Minnesota; Northwest Angle; Angle Township; Lake of the Woods County, Minnesota; Magnusens Island; Angle Inlet, Minnesota; Penasse, Minnesota\n- Radio stations: KKWQ-FM; KRWB (AM)\n- Companies: Border Broadcasting\n- Historic sites: Fort Saint Charles\n\nFacts:\n- KKWQ-FM 92.5 is a small local radio station that broadcasts from Warroad, Minnesota, a border town.\n- The Northwest Angle, called the Angle by locals, is coextensive with Angle Township and is part of northern Lake of the Woods County, Minnesota.\n- KRWB (AM) is owned and operated by Border Broadcasting, which also owns sister station KKWQ-FM.\n- Fort Saint Charles was located on Magnusens Island in the Northwest Angle of Minnesota, 3.5 miles east of Angle Inlet, Minnesota, and one mile southwest of Penasse, Minnesota, the state's most northerly point.",
